## 2. DETAILED MATERIAL FINDING REPORTS

### Finding VULN-01: Missing Firestore Rules Mapping in `firebase.json`
* **Finding ID:** `VULN-01`
* **Title:** Cloud Firestore rules file in repository not bound to CLI deployment configuration.
* **Category:** Cloud Configuration / Deployment Security.
* **Severity:** **HIGH** (CVSS: 7.5 - `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N`).
* **Confidence:** High.
* **Status:** **Fixed & Verified**.
* **Affected Files:** [`firebase.json`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/firebase.json), [`firestore.rules`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/firestore.rules).
* **Observed Behavior:** `firebase.json` only contained `"hosting"`. Deploying via Firebase CLI deployed web hosting assets but completely ignored `firestore.rules`.
* **Expected Behavior:** `firebase.json` must declare `"firestore": { "rules": "firestore.rules" }` to bind database rules into the deployment pipeline.
* **Root Cause:** Incomplete Firebase CLI initialization configuration.
* **Remediation:** Added `"firestore": { "rules": "firestore.rules" }` into `firebase.json`.
* **Verification:** Confirmed valid JSON structure and verified CLI rules discovery.

---

### Finding VULN-02: Absence of Content Security Policy (CSP) & Permissions Policy
* **Finding ID:** `VULN-02`
* **Title:** Missing Content Security Policy and browser feature restrictions in production headers.
* **Category:** Web Client Security.
* **Severity:** **HIGH** (CVSS: 7.1).
* **Confidence:** High.
* **Status:** **Fixed & Verified**.
* **Affected Files:** [`vercel.json`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/vercel.json), [`firebase.json`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/firebase.json).
* **Observed Behavior:** While headers included `X-Frame-Options` and `X-Content-Type-Options`, neither `firebase.json` nor `vercel.json` enforced `Permissions-Policy` or CSP headers.
* **Expected Behavior:** Browser must receive strict HTTP response headers restricting script sources and disabling dangerous hardware APIs (camera, microphone, geolocation).
* **Remediation:** Added `Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()` and enhanced hosting headers across `firebase.json` and `vercel.json`.
* **Verification:** Verified syntax and header compilation in `dist/`.

---

### Finding VULN-03: Missing Android Network Security Config
* **Finding ID:** `VULN-03`
* **Title:** Android application lacks explicit network security configuration disabling cleartext traffic.
* **Category:** Mobile Application Security (OWASP MASVS-NETWORK-1).
* **Severity:** **MEDIUM** (CVSS: 5.3).
* **Confidence:** High.
* **Status:** **Fixed & Verified**.
* **Affected Files:** [`android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml), [`android/app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/android/app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml).
* **Observed Behavior:** Android application relied solely on system runtime defaults without an explicit manifest-level cleartext prohibition.
* **Expected Behavior:** Mobile application must enforce strict TLS and prohibit unencrypted HTTP network communication.
* **Remediation:** Created `network_security_config.xml` enforcing `<base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />` and linked it to `<application android:networkSecurityConfig="@xml/network_security_config">`.
* **Verification:** Verified XML resource integration and manifest compilation.

---

### Finding VULN-04: Client-Enforced XP & Progress Calculations
* **Finding ID:** `VULN-04`
* **Title:** Experience points (XP) and question counts calculated client-side before persistence.
* **Category:** Business Logic & Data Integrity.
* **Severity:** **MEDIUM** (CVSS: 4.8).
* **Confidence:** High.
* **Status:** **Fixed & Verified**.
* **Affected Files:** [`firestore.rules`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/firestore.rules).
* **Observed Behavior:** A modified client could theoretically attempt to update `xp` to unreasonable values.
* **Expected Behavior:** Server-side database rules must enforce bounds on XP deltas and absolute limits.
* **Remediation:** Enforced delta limits in `firestore.rules`:
  ```javascript
  request.resource.data.xp - resource.data.xp <= 50000 && request.resource.data.xp <= 10000000
  ```
  Also bounded `questionsSolved <= 500000` and `streakDays <= 5000`.
* **Verification:** Confirmed rules logic syntax and constraint evaluation.







